    "narrative": "Our lineup is anchored by **Cal Raleigh** (78.02), who draws an ideal matchup against Springs and his elevated 4.84 xERA. The combination of his power profile, current form, and the plus-park environment makes him our elite play today. **Lawrence Butler** (72.57) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) also grade out as strong starts. **Beavers** is particularly enticing; despite facing a veteran like Scherzer, his leadoff spot and a favorable 5.10 xERA matchup offer massive upside, especially with a \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor boosting his stolen base probability\u2014a critical component in our pursuit of the scarcest 5x5 category. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.58) and **Kyle Karros** (60.59) are set to capitalize on similar efficiency indicators, with **Karros** benefiting from a soft matchup against Valdez and improved stolen base potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Yainer Diaz** (41.14) on the bench. He was the final cut, as his projected efficiency against Rasmussen simply could not surpass the platoon-advantaged upside of **Daulton Varsho**. While **Diaz** remains a reliable asset, the current optimizer data favors **Varsho**\u2019s specific split-advantage in today's conditions. We must also exercise caution with **Bryce Harper** (49.40); facing a high-caliber arm like Sale is a distinct risk that suppresses his ceiling today, though we are keeping him active for his reliable counting stats. We have opted to sit **JJ Bleday** and **Gleyber Torres** entirely, as their projected production against their respective opponents fails to clear the threshold required to protect our limited remaining game caps. Every roster decision today is focused on maximizing daily efficiency to maintain our edge in a tight Roto race.",
